<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kinzig (Rhine)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kinzig is a river of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-forest">Black Forest</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, flowing west through Wolfach, Haslach, Gengenbach and Offenburg to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kehl">Kehl</a>. Its valley has long been one of the main routes across the Black Forest. Offenburg and Gengenbach grew at its crossings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kinzig-rhine.jpg" alt="Kinzig (Rhine)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marion Schneider &amp; Christoph Aistleitner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kinzig_292.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
